1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
What if ten suns rose at once

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,600
and scorched the earth?

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:07,180
Chinese legend says they abandoned their usual

4
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:07,848
turns.

5
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:10,640
Rivers dried, crops burned,

6
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:14,700
and ordinary people suffered under relentless heat.

7
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,320
The earth could not survive ten heavens

8
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:18,370
burning at once.

9
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:22,840
Hunters, farmers, and animals searched in vain

10
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:24,220
for water or shade.

11
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,260
Hou Yi raised his bow.

12
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:29,200
He was asked to restore balance where

13
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:31,920
power from above had scorched the world

14
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:32,478
below.

15
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,200
He shot down nine suns,

16
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:36,460
one after another.

17
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,580
Each impact dimmed the sky until only

18
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:41,740
the light the world needed remained.

19
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,300
With a single sun moving overhead,

20
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,160
crops could grow again.

21
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,040
Water returned to land that had nearly

22
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:50,980
become desert.

23
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:54,440
The hero did not make the world

24
00:00:54,450 --> 00:00:56,820
safe by destroying all power.

25
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,360
He made it livable by leaving enough

26
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:00,300
and no more.
